SNES Touch changes to wasm-dolphin (github.com/dougchansan/wasm-dolphin, commit 7e38409), GPLv2+.
Build: npm run fetch:dolphin && npm run patch:upstream, apply this patch, add '_SetInputStateForPort' after '_SetInputState' in the EXPORTED_FUNCTIONS of vendor/dolphin/Source/Core/Core/CMakeLists.txt, then configure:upstream and build:upstream:full-core (Emscripten 5.0.7).
The JavaScript changes (src/upstream-worker-adapter.js, src/upstream-discio-worker.js, src/upstream-worker-protocol.js, src/core-host.js) are marked 'SNES Touch' in the files themselves.

What the C++ changes do:
- core/upstream: controllers in all four ports and a SetInputStateForPort export (players 2-4); tools: a macOS toolchain branch.
- vendor/dolphin CachedInterpreter.cpp (shipped whole in SNES-TOUCH-SOURCES/, marked SNES Touch): the PowerPC-to-WASM JIT routed mcrf (opcode 19, SUBOP10 0) to the condition-register logic emitter and produced invalid WebAssembly, it now takes the fallback path; ps_sum0/1, ps_sel, fsel, ps_div, ps_neg/mr/abs/nabs and the integer psq_l formats are compiled natively instead of ending the block; stw/sth/stb into the write-gather pipe page go straight into the pipe; compiled blocks are dispatched directly (DOLPHIN_WEB_DIRECT_WASM_BLOCK_DISPATCH=1); blocks run on past conditional branches (side exits), and a block that branches back to its own start loops inside WebAssembly while its cycle budget lasts (?sideexit=0 and ?wasmloop=0 turn these off; src/core-host.js).
- vendor/dolphin Interpreter_FPUtils.h (shipped whole in SNES-TOUCH-SOURCES/, marked SNES Touch): the fused multiply-adds skip the software fma that WebAssembly falls back to when the product is exact in double precision, which gives the same bits.
- vendor/dolphin VideoCommon: the WebGPU backend had been exempted from Dolphin's depth conversion for backends without a reversible depth range (fog depth, per-pixel depth, depth copies, EFB peeks and pokes, clear depth), but its vertex shader writes a reversed depth buffer, so those exemptions fed inverted depth into the fog formula and fogged everything near the camera to the fog colour (a black screen in Need for Speed: Underground 2). The standard conversion is restored.

